    {
      "id": "claim_aa9f7b740c584f86bcffc9d418742533",
      "statement": "The Python and Rust backends produce identical multi-span output: Python populates match_blocks through _consolidate_match_blocks on the detailed traceback in src/cite_right/core/aligner_py.py, and Rust populates them through smith_waterman_match_blocks / align_batch_with_match_blocks in rust_core/src/smith_waterman.rs (exposed as align_pair_blocks_details / align_batch_blocks_details). The contract tests compare match_blocks and full multi-span citation output, so backend choice does not change which spans are returned.",
